{
  "title": "First conjugation: present tense",
  "note": "Verbs are listed by infinitive. First-conjugation verbs end in -are: amare, to love. Drop -re for the stem ama-, then add the endings: amo, amas, amat, amamus, amatis, amant (I love, you love, he/she loves, we love, you all love, they love). In amo the a merges into the o.",
  "src": {
    "t": "Allen and Greenough, The Four Conjugations",
    "u": "https://dcc.dickinson.edu/grammar/latin/four-conjugations"
  },
